index 15a1ad5180aa16670a2a709f6adfe61142b50321..9dc0d3415b87a7e619baca72accf1e319b27b683 100644
--- a/docs/subsystems/gui-shell.md
+++ b/docs/subsystems/gui-shell.md
@@ -1095,0 +1096,6 @@ saves, narrow layouts and all five languages in Chromium and WebKit.
+
+### Embedded web runtime
+
+`magpie web --embedded --data-dir <absolute> --addr 127.0.0.1:<port> --no-open` is intended for a host-managed runtime. It requires a distinct loopback `MAGPIE_ADDR`, `MAGPIE_WEB_KEY`, `MAGPIE_EMBEDDED_GATEWAY_KEY`, and a per-process `MAGPIE_EMBEDDED_INSTANCE_ID` (the last two at least 16 characters). The management key uses the normal web session; the inference key is required on gateway requests, including loopback. The gateway key does not isolate processes running as the same OS user.
+
+`GET /api/integration` identifies the API as `magpie`, API version 1, with its version, embedded flag, instance ID, and capabilities. Authenticated inference route `GET /v1/magpie/integration` returns the same identity, so the host can check that both ports belong to the process it started. Port 0 is refused; both ports must be explicitly selected. Embedded management only exposes selected provider, group, account and sign-in operations. Agent management and self-update are unavailable. Only Codex sign-in and explicitly requested file-backed Codex account discovery are supported in embedded mode. A selected shared Codex file is read in place; when its token expires, Codex must renew it. Other subscription sign-ins are unavailable. The gateway accepts only model discovery, Claude messages and token counting, chat completions, Responses, and the identity endpoint; it refuses MCP, image, file and administrative routes. A host keeps stdin open while it owns the runtime; EOF stops the web and gateway listeners. This mode is not an operating-system filesystem sandbox. Hosts must own the binary, ports, data directory, credentials and lifecycle. This contract is experimental until its startup and provider paths are independently verified.
diff --git a/docs/subsystems/providers-accounts.md b/docs/subsystems/providers-accounts.md
index cc6b5f30d804774591f93e709a1bebbf6ae0ac0d..5379182b179f3a5dc4335308a1932dd424f47788 100644
--- a/docs/subsystems/providers-accounts.md
+++ b/docs/subsystems/providers-accounts.md
@@ -15,0 +16,30 @@ keys and accounts per request is in [Gateway routing and fallback](gateway-routi
+## Embedded Codex accounts
+
+In embedded mode, the legacy account-discovery paths stay disabled. The
+runtime can sign in to Codex through the browser OAuth flow and keeps that
+sign-in under its private data directory in `codex/auth.json`. Private
+credential and selection-record operations use an opened `os.Root` and reject
+symlinked stores. Refreshing an owned sign-in updates that private file. Other built-in and plugin sign-in
+flows are not available through this embedded account path.
+
+On an explicit discovery request, `DiscoverEmbeddedCodexSources` looks for
+file-backed Codex sign-ins and returns account metadata and a canonical source
+reference. `SelectEmbeddedCodexSource` records the selected reference under
+the private data directory; it does not copy credentials. Requests read the
+selected file without modifying it. If its access token needs renewal, the
+request fails and the user must renew the sign-in in Codex. Keychain and
+symlinked credential files are not supported by this discovery path. Privacy
+settings and a pre-existing `MAGPIE_NO_ACCOUNTS` disable these embedded flows.
+Standalone account behavior is unchanged.
+
+The embedded account uses the model list fetched from the Codex backend and
+stored under the private data directory, keyed by account and source. Model
+instructions use the same account-specific boundary. It does not read the user's Codex
+model cache or install a helper. A model refresh makes a network request; a
+missing saved list is not treated as evidence that a model is supported.
+
+Sources: [`embedded_codex.go`](../../internal/provider/embedded_codex.go),
+[`embedded_codex_sources.go`](../../internal/provider/embedded_codex_sources.go),
+[`signin.go`](../../internal/provider/signin.go), and
+[`embedded_codex_test.go`](../../internal/provider/embedded_codex_test.go).
+
